I. Introduction

This is the main README file for Alatar.

Alatar is disigned to be a game engine play the games Wizard and Ultimate
Wizard from the Commodore 64 on a modern computer.  This distribution does NOT
include any files from the original games.  You will need to have a copy of one
of these two games, or additonal level files to be able to play the game with
this software.

Alatar has two modes of operation, one uses the original graphics and the other
uses updated graphics.  The original graphics data files will need to be
extracted from the original game to use this mode of game play.  The updated
graphics are included in this distribution and can be used with just the level
files from the game.

Currently Alatar only builds under Linux.  It should not be that difficult to
port it to another platform such as Windows or MacOS but that has not yet been
incorporated.

II. Building Alatar

II.A. Dependancies

Alatar requires the following supporting software to be avalaible to build:

  o SDL2 <https://www.libsdl.org/>
  o SDL2 Image <https://www.libsdl.org/projects/old/SDL_image/>
  o GLEW <https://glew.sourceforge.net/>
  o FreeType <https://freetype.org/>
  o CMake <https://cmake.org/>
  o stb_image <https://github.com/nothings/stb>
  
If you're running Ubuntu or a related distribuiotns the commands in the
following sections will install the required files:

II.A.1. SDL2

sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install libsdl2-2.0
sudo apt-get install libsdl2-dev

II.A.2. SDL2 Image

sudo apt-get install libsdl2-image-2.0
sudo apt-get install libsdl2-image-dev

II.A.3. GLEW

sudo apt-get install libglew2.2
sudo apt-get install libglew-dev

II.A.4. FreeType

sudo apt-get install libfreetype6
sudo apt-get install libfreetype-dev

II.A.5. CMake

sudo apt-get install cmake

II.A.6. stb_image

The files required from stb_image are included in this distribution and are
lisenced in the public domain.  For more information visit
https://github.com/nothings/stb

II.B. Compiling

Alatar is built using CMake.  Change the current directory to the root of the
Alatar directory and use the following commands to build the executables.

cd build
cd cmake ..
make

II.C. Installing

At the current time it is assumed there is a directory at the same level as the
executables callsed resources.  Within the resources directory there are three
sub directories classic, shaders, and updated.  The classic directory continans
files from the original game that are needed to run with the original graphics
(see below).  The shaders directory contains the glsl shaders used for display.
Updated contains the grpahics used for the updated graphics display mode.

